# Local-only agent guidance (not published; comments in tracked files must not
# reference these)
CLAUDE.md
RULES.md
task.md
PLAN.md
.claude/

# The author's own captures of the four channels. They are the product, not a
# working set — the plug-in has no capture browser and loads these and only
# these — and they are deliberately NOT published with the source: the code is
# MIT, a capture is a recording rather than source, and the two are not the same
# grant. Tracked source still names them by path, because the four channel banks
# are resolved that way and there is nothing else they could be called.
#
# A clone without them configures with an actionable error naming
# RATIONS_CAPTURES_DIR; see CMakeLists.txt.
captures/

# Personal CMake configure presets (local reference-tree paths).
CMakeUserPresets.json

# Build directories
build/
build-*/
cmake-build-*/

# CMake generated
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
Makefile
*.cmake
!CMakeLists.txt
# ...but cmake/ holds SOURCE scripts, not generated ones — the MinGW toolchain
# file lives there and is named on the configure command line, so without this
# negation the blanket *.cmake above would keep it out of a fresh clone and the
# Windows build would be unreproducible. Generated .cmake files all live under
# the build directories already ignored above.
!cmake/*.cmake

# Compiled output
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.so.*
*.vst3

# Release archives produced by scripts/makedist-linux.sh — these are attached
# to GitHub releases, not committed.
dist/
*.tar.gz
*.tar.xz
*.zip

# Debug info
*.pdb
*.dSYM/

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.clangd/
compile_commands.json

